18:09.840 --> 18:17.680
until I mean, he went with Camara, with the Trident being kind of OP. But I think he very

18:17.680 --> 18:22.880
much is kind of the main Red Bull talent at the moment. And in F2, he has been, I mean,

18:22.880 --> 18:28.560
despite having bad luck, he's still leading the championship, and I expect to see more of him

18:28.560 --> 18:32.880
upfront this weekend in Canada. And speaking of drivers who went from

18:32.880 --> 18:39.760
F4 straight to F3, I think this leads us on perfectly to Fionn McLaughlin, who is in his

18:39.760 --> 18:46.320
rookie season in F3. He won British F4 last year, also in his rookie season. He struggled a bit

18:46.320 --> 18:55.440
during Formula Regional Oceania earlier this year, and he is currently P18 in the F3 Championship.

18:55.440 --> 19:01.760
Obviously, again, it's only been one round, so we can't really judge too heavily. But he has been

19:01.760 --> 19:08.960
struggling, and like we saw with Tsolov, it might take some time before he gets back on his feet.

19:09.520 --> 19:13.760
But I do rate him, and I do hope to see him do well eventually.

19:14.400 --> 19:18.400
I think it would be more of a case where this season it would be more him kind of getting used

19:18.400 --> 19:24.880
to things, and we'll see more of him next year, and maybe towards the end of this year. Next year,

